@push('styles')

<style>
  :root {
    --ground: #FFFFFF;
    --surface: #FFFFFF;
    --surface-2: #EEF2F7;
    --ink: #14213A;
    --ink-2: #43506B;
    --muted: #6B7793;
    --line: #E1E7EF;
    --navy: #12294B;
    --navy-2: #1D3B6B;
    --accent: #E08A3C;
    --accent-ink: #B5651D;
    --accent-soft: #FBEEDF;
    --teal: #1F8A7A;
    --teal-soft: #E2F1EE;
    --icon-tile: #FFFFFF;
    --radius: 14px;
    --shadow: 0 1px 2px rgba(18,41,75,.05), 0 8px 24px rgba(18,41,75,.06);
    --mono: ui-monospace, "SF Mono", "Cascadia Code", "Roboto Mono", Menlo, Consolas, monospace;
    --sans: "Segoe UI", system-ui, -apple-system, "Helvetica Neue", Arial, sans-serif;
  }
  /* This page deliberately commits to a single light look — no dark-mode overrides, so it stays
     white whether the viewer's browser/OS is in light or dark mode. */
  :root { color-scheme: light; }

  * { box-sizing: border-box; }
  body { margin: 0; background: var(--ground); color: var(--ink); font-family: var(--sans); line-height: 1.6; -webkit-font-smoothing: antialiased; }
  .wrap { max-width: 1180px; margin: 0 auto; padding: 0 24px; }
  /* Keep prose readable even on a wide container */
  .lead, .sec-intro { max-width: 68ch; }

  /* ---- Header ---- */
  .top {
    background:
      radial-gradient(1200px 400px at 15% -30%, rgba(224,138,60,.18), transparent 60%),
      linear-gradient(160deg, var(--navy) 0%, var(--navy-2) 100%);
    color: #EAF0F8; padding: 56px 0 60px;
  }
  .brandrow { display: flex; align-items: center; gap: 14px; margin-bottom: 28px; }
  .mark { width: 42px; height: 42px; border-radius: 11px; flex: none; background: var(--icon-tile); display: grid; place-items: center; box-shadow: 0 4px 14px rgba(0,0,0,.25); overflow: hidden; }
  .mark img { width: 100%; height: 100%; object-fit: contain; }
  .brandname { font-weight: 600; font-size: 15px; letter-spacing: .2px; }
  .brandtag { font-size: 12.5px; color: #9FB0CB; }
  .eyebrow { text-transform: uppercase; letter-spacing: 1.5px; font-size: 12px; color: var(--accent); font-weight: 600; margin: 0 0 12px; }
  h1 { font-size: clamp(30px, 5vw, 44px); line-height: 1.12; margin: 0 0 14px; font-weight: 700; letter-spacing: -.5px; text-wrap: balance; max-width: 18ch; }
  .lead { font-size: 17px; color: #C6D2E5; margin: 0 0 26px; max-width: 56ch; }
  .jump { display: flex; flex-wrap: wrap; gap: 10px; }
  .jump a { font-size: 13px; color: #EAF0F8; text-decoration: none; background: rgba(255,255,255,.08); border: 1px solid rgba(255,255,255,.14); padding: 7px 13px; border-radius: 999px; transition: background .15s; }
  .jump a:hover { background: rgba(255,255,255,.16); }

  /* ---- Section scaffolding ---- */
  section { padding: 42px 0; scroll-margin-top: 20px; }
  section + section { border-top: 1px solid var(--line); }
  .sec-label { text-transform: uppercase; letter-spacing: 1.4px; font-size: 12px; color: var(--muted); font-weight: 700; margin: 0 0 6px; display: block; }
  h2 { font-size: 23px; margin: 0 0 6px; letter-spacing: -.3px; font-weight: 700; }
  .sec-intro { margin: 0 0 22px; color: var(--ink-2); font-size: 14.5px; max-width: 62ch; }

  /* ---- Scope cards ---- */
  .scopes { display: grid; grid-template-columns: repeat(3, 1fr); gap: 16px; }
  .scope { background: var(--surface); border: 1px solid var(--line); border-radius: var(--radius); padding: 20px; box-shadow: var(--shadow); }
  .scope h3 { margin: 0 0 4px; font-size: 15.5px; }
  .scope p { margin: 0 0 14px; font-size: 13.5px; color: var(--ink-2); }
  .chiplabel { font-size: 11.5px; color: var(--muted); margin: 0 0 5px; font-weight: 600; letter-spacing: .3px; }
  .cmd { font-family: var(--mono); font-size: 13px; background: var(--surface-2); border: 1px solid var(--line); border-radius: 8px; padding: 7px 10px; color: var(--ink); display: inline-block; word-break: break-word; }
  .cmd b { color: var(--accent-ink); font-weight: 700; }

  /* ---- Chat preview ---- */
  .chat { background: var(--surface); border: 1px solid var(--line); border-radius: var(--radius); padding: 22px; box-shadow: var(--shadow); max-width: 580px; }
  .bubble { display: flex; gap: 10px; margin-bottom: 16px; }
  .bubble:last-child { margin-bottom: 0; }
  .ava { width: 30px; height: 30px; border-radius: 8px; flex: none; display: grid; place-items: center; overflow: hidden; }
  .ava.user { background: var(--surface-2); color: var(--muted); }
  .ava.bot { background: var(--icon-tile); }
  .ava.bot img { width: 100%; height: 100%; object-fit: contain; }
  .msg { flex: 1; }
  .who { font-size: 12px; color: var(--muted); font-weight: 600; margin-bottom: 3px; }
  .say { background: var(--surface-2); border: 1px solid var(--line); border-radius: 4px 12px 12px 12px; padding: 11px 14px; font-size: 14px; color: var(--ink); }
  .bubble.you .say { background: var(--accent-soft); border-color: transparent; }
  .say .toprow { margin-bottom: 6px; }
  .say ul { margin: 8px 0 0; padding-left: 18px; }
  .say li { margin: 3px 0; }
  .say code { font-family: var(--mono); font-size: 12.5px; background: rgba(18,41,75,.06); padding: 1px 5px; border-radius: 5px; }
  .say a { color: var(--teal); font-weight: 600; text-decoration: none; }
  .say a:hover { text-decoration: underline; }

  /* ---- Command groups ---- */
  .cmdgroup { background: var(--surface); border: 1px solid var(--line); border-radius: var(--radius); box-shadow: var(--shadow); margin-bottom: 18px; overflow: hidden; }
  /* On wide screens, flow command groups into two columns so the page uses the space. */
  .cmdgrid { display: grid; gap: 18px; grid-template-columns: 1fr; align-items: start; }
  .cmdgrid .cmdgroup { margin-bottom: 0; }
  @media (min-width: 900px) { .cmdgrid { grid-template-columns: 1fr 1fr; } .cmdgrid .span-2 { grid-column: 1 / -1; } }
  .cmdgroup > .gh { display: flex; align-items: center; gap: 12px; padding: 16px 20px; border-bottom: 1px solid var(--line); background: var(--surface-2); }
  .gh .gi { width: 34px; height: 34px; border-radius: 9px; flex: none; display: grid; place-items: center; background: var(--icon-tile); border: 1px solid var(--line); overflow: hidden; }
  .gh .gi img { width: 21px; height: 21px; object-fit: contain; display: block; }
  .gh h3 { margin: 0; font-size: 16px; }
  .gh .gsub { margin: 1px 0 0; font-size: 12.5px; color: var(--muted); }
  .tablewrap { overflow-x: auto; }
  table { width: 100%; border-collapse: collapse; background: var(--surface); font-size: 14px; min-width: 480px; }
  th, td { text-align: left; padding: 12px 20px; border-bottom: 1px solid var(--line); vertical-align: top; }
  tbody tr:last-child td { border-bottom: none; }
  td.c code { font-family: var(--mono); font-size: 12.5px; color: var(--accent-ink); font-weight: 600; white-space: nowrap; display: inline-block; }
  td.c .alt { color: var(--muted); font-weight: 400; font-size: 11.5px; }
  td.c { width: 45%; }
  td.d { color: var(--ink-2); }

  .note { font-size: 13px; color: var(--muted); margin: 14px 2px 0; }
  .note b { color: var(--ink-2); }

  /* ---- FAQ ---- */
  .faq { display: grid; gap: 10px; }
  details { background: var(--surface); border: 1px solid var(--line); border-radius: 12px; box-shadow: var(--shadow); overflow: hidden; }
  summary { cursor: pointer; list-style: none; padding: 16px 20px; font-weight: 600; font-size: 15px; display: flex; justify-content: space-between; align-items: center; gap: 12px; }
  summary::-webkit-details-marker { display: none; }
  summary::after { content: "+"; color: var(--accent-ink); font-size: 20px; font-weight: 400; flex: none; }
  details[open] summary::after { content: "\2013"; }
  details > p { margin: 0; padding: 0 20px 18px; color: var(--ink-2); font-size: 14px; }
  details > p code { font-family: var(--mono); font-size: 12.5px; background: var(--surface-2); padding: 1px 5px; border-radius: 5px; color: var(--accent-ink); }
  details a { color: var(--teal); font-weight: 600; text-decoration: none; }
  details a:hover { text-decoration: underline; }

  /* ---- Info strip ---- */
  .strip { display: grid; grid-template-columns: 1fr 1fr; gap: 16px; }
  .infocard { background: var(--surface); border: 1px solid var(--line); border-radius: var(--radius); padding: 20px; box-shadow: var(--shadow); }
  .infocard.teal { border-left: 3px solid var(--teal); }
  .infocard.pitch { border-left: 3px solid var(--accent); }
  .infocard h3 { margin: 0 0 7px; font-size: 15px; }
  .infocard p { margin: 0; font-size: 13.5px; color: var(--ink-2); }
  .infocard a { color: var(--teal); font-weight: 600; text-decoration: none; }
  .infocard.pitch a { color: var(--accent-ink); }
  .infocard a:hover { text-decoration: underline; }

  /* ---- Footer ---- */
  footer { border-top: 1px solid var(--line); padding: 30px 0 48px; color: var(--muted); font-size: 13px; }
  footer a { color: var(--ink-2); text-decoration: none; }
  footer a:hover { text-decoration: underline; }

  @media (max-width: 680px) {
    .scopes { grid-template-columns: 1fr; }
    .strip { grid-template-columns: 1fr; }
    td.c { width: auto; }
  }
</style>
@endpush

@section('content')

<header class="top">
  <div class="wrap">
    <div class="brandrow">
      <div class="mark"><img src="data:image/png;base64," alt="Mela"></div>
      <div>
        <div class="brandname">Mela Meeting Assistant</div>
        <div class="brandtag">Help &amp; Commands</div>
      </div>
    </div>
    <p class="eyebrow">Help Center</p>
    <h1 class="text-light">Everything Mela can do</h1>
    <p class="lead">Mela joins your Microsoft Teams meetings to transcribe the conversation and hand you a clean summary afterward — and it can also help with your inbox, calendar, and meeting prep. Here's the full guide.</p>
    <nav class="jump">
      <a href="#reach">How to reach Mela</a>
      <a href="#meeting">In the meeting</a>
      <a href="#after">After the meeting</a>
      <a href="#work">Inbox &amp; calendar</a>
      <a href="#faq">FAQ</a>
      <a href="#support">Support</a>
    </nav>
  </div>
</header>

<main class="wrap">

  <!-- ============ HOW TO REACH ============ -->
  <section id="reach">
    <span class="sec-label">Getting a response</span>
    <h2>How to reach Mela</h2>
    <p class="sec-intro">Whether you need to mention Mela depends on where you're chatting. The word <code class="cmd" style="padding:1px 6px"><b>@mela</b></code> is only needed where Teams requires it.</p>
    <div class="scopes">
      <div class="scope">
        <h3>Direct chat</h3>
        <p>One-on-one with the bot. No mention needed — just type the command.</p>
        <p class="chiplabel">EXAMPLE</p>
        <span class="cmd">help</span>
      </div>
      <div class="scope">
        <h3>Group chat</h3>
        <p>Works with or without mentioning Mela.</p>
        <p class="chiplabel">EXAMPLE</p>
        <span class="cmd">help</span> &nbsp;or&nbsp; <span class="cmd"><b>@mela</b> help</span>
      </div>
      <div class="scope">
        <h3>Team channel</h3>
        <p>Channels only deliver messages that mention the bot — so mention Mela first.</p>
        <p class="chiplabel">EXAMPLE</p>
        <span class="cmd"><b>@mela</b> help</span>
      </div>
    </div>
    <p class="note"><b>Tip:</b> Mela understands natural language, so you don't have to match the wording exactly — "can you join this call?" works just as well as "please join."</p>
  </section>

  <!-- ============ HELP REPLY PREVIEW ============ -->
  <section id="preview">
    <span class="sec-label">What it looks like</span>
    <h2>The help reply, in chat</h2>
    <p class="sec-intro">Type <code class="cmd" style="padding:1px 6px">help</code> anytime and Mela replies with the essentials and a link back to this page.</p>
    <div class="chat">
      <div class="bubble you">
        <div class="ava user"><svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" width="16" height="16" fill="currentColor" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M12 12a5 5 0 1 0 0-10 5 5 0 0 0 0 10zm0 2c-4.4 0-8 2.2-8 5v1h16v-1c0-2.8-3.6-5-8-5z"/></svg></div>
        <div class="msg">
          <div class="who">You</div>
          <div class="say">help</div>
        </div>
      </div>
      <div class="bubble">
        <div class="ava bot"><img src="data:image/png;base64," alt="Mela"></div>
        <div class="msg">
          <div class="who">Mela Meeting Assistant</div>
          <div class="say">
            <div class="toprow">Hi - I'm <strong>Mela Meeting Assistant</strong>. I join your Teams meetings to transcribe them and send you a summary afterward.</div>
            <div><strong>In a meeting, type:</strong></div>
            <ul>
              <li><code>@mela please join</code> - start recording</li>
              <li><code>@mela please leave</code> - stop recording</li>
              <li><code>@mela what did last person say</code> - live meeting notes</li>
              <li><code>@mela summarize</code>, <code>generate minutes</code>, or <code>fetch transcript</code></li>
            </ul>
            <div style="margin-top:10px">In a direct chat you can drop the <code>@mela</code>.<br>
            Full guide -&gt; <a target="_blank" href="/mela-meeting-assistant/help" >/mela-meeting-assistant/help</a></div>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- ============ IN THE MEETING ============ -->
  <section id="meeting">
    <span class="sec-label">Command reference</span>
    <h2>In the meeting</h2>
    <p class="sec-intro">Live controls you use while a meeting is happening. In the meeting chat, mention Mela first (<code class="cmd" style="padding:1px 6px"><b>@mela</b></code>).</p>

    <div class="cmdgrid">
    <div class="cmdgroup">
      <div class="gh"><div class="gi"><img src="data:image/png;base64," alt="Teams"></div><div><h3>Recording</h3><p class="gsub">Start, pause, and stop transcription</p></div></div>
      <div class="tablewrap"><table><tbody>
        <tr><td class="c"><code>@mela please join</code></td><td class="d">Bring Mela into the meeting you're in and start recording. Mela announces itself so everyone knows the meeting is being transcribed.</td></tr>
        <tr><td class="c"><code>@mela pause recording</code></td><td class="d">Temporarily stop taking notes for a private moment. Mela reminds you after 5 minutes if it's still paused.</td></tr>
        <tr><td class="c"><code>@mela unpause recording</code></td><td class="d">Resume taking notes after a pause.</td></tr>
        <tr><td class="c"><code>@mela please leave</code><br><span class="alt">or <code>@mela leave</code></span></td><td class="d">Stop recording and remove Mela from the meeting. Either phrasing works.</td></tr>
      </tbody></table></div>
    </div>

    <div class="cmdgroup">
      <div class="gh"><div class="gi"><img src="data:image/png;base64," alt="Chat"></div><div><h3>Live questions</h3><p class="gsub">Ask about what's being said right now</p></div></div>
      <div class="tablewrap"><table><tbody>
        <tr><td class="c"><code>@mela what did last person say</code></td><td class="d">Catch up on the most recent thing said — great if you missed a moment. You can add detail: "what did the last person say about the deadline."</td></tr>
        <tr><td class="c"><code>@mela what did [name] say about [topic]</code></td><td class="d">Ask what a specific person said about a specific subject during the meeting.</td></tr>
      </tbody></table></div>
    </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- ============ AFTER THE MEETING ============ -->
  <section id="after">
    <span class="sec-label">Command reference</span>
    <h2>After the meeting</h2>
    <p class="sec-intro">Turn a finished meeting into notes you can share. Ask for these in your chat with Mela anytime.</p>

    <div class="cmdgroup">
      <div class="gh"><div class="gi"><img src="data:image/png;base64," alt="Mela"></div><div><h3>Notes &amp; outputs</h3><p class="gsub">Generate a summary, minutes, or transcript</p></div></div>
      <div class="tablewrap"><table><tbody>
        <tr><td class="c"><code>summarize</code></td><td class="d">Get a concise recap of what was discussed.</td></tr>
        <tr><td class="c"><code>generate minutes</code></td><td class="d">Get formal meeting minutes — decisions and action items.</td></tr>
        <tr><td class="c"><code>fetch transcript</code></td><td class="d">Get the full word-for-word transcript of the meeting.</td></tr>
        <tr><td class="c"><code>send me the executive summary</code><br><span class="alt">or <code>exec summary</code> / <code>one-pager</code></span></td><td class="d">Get a one-page executive summary — TL;DR, key decisions, action items, risks, and next steps — emailed <strong>privately to you</strong>, not posted in the chat. Works <strong>mid-call</strong> too: ask during the meeting and Mela builds it from the transcript captured so far.</td></tr>
        <tr><td class="c"><code>meeting overview</code></td><td class="d">Get an overview of a past meeting you attended (e.g. "what happened in my last meeting").</td></tr>
        <tr><td class="c"><code>key takeaways</code></td><td class="d">Get the highlights and main points.</td></tr>
        <tr><td class="c"><code>what did we decide about [topic]</code></td><td class="d">Ask a specific question about the meeting's content.</td></tr>
      </tbody></table></div>
    </div>
    <p class="note"><b>Send it onward:</b> add "…and email it to me" to any of the above, or say <b>send the last summary to my email</b>, and Mela delivers it to your inbox.</p>
  </section>

  <!-- ============ INBOX & CALENDAR ============ -->
  <section id="work">
    <span class="sec-label">Command reference</span>
    <h2>Inbox &amp; calendar</h2>
    <p class="sec-intro">Beyond meetings, Mela can help you stay on top of email and your schedule.</p>

    <div class="cmdgrid">
    <div class="cmdgroup">
      <div class="gh"><div class="gi"><img src="data:image/png;base64," alt="Outlook"></div><div><h3>Email &amp; inbox</h3><p class="gsub">Review, reply, draft, and send</p></div></div>
      <div class="tablewrap"><table><tbody>
        <tr><td class="c"><code>check my inbox</code></td><td class="d">Review recent or urgent messages (e.g. "show urgent emails", "what did Marin send me").</td></tr>
        <tr><td class="c"><code>reply to [name]</code></td><td class="d">Draft a reply to an email or thread.</td></tr>
        <tr><td class="c"><code>draft an email</code></td><td class="d">Write a new email, invitation, or sample message.</td></tr>
        <tr><td class="c"><code>send it to my email</code></td><td class="d">Send the last summary, transcript, or minutes to your inbox.</td></tr>
      </tbody></table></div>
    </div>

    <div class="cmdgroup">
      <div class="gh"><div class="gi"><img src="data:image/png;base64," alt="Planner"></div><div><h3>Calendar &amp; prep</h3><p class="gsub">See your schedule and get meeting-ready</p></div></div>
      <div class="tablewrap"><table><tbody>
        <tr><td class="c"><code>what meetings do I have today</code></td><td class="d">View your schedule or check availability (e.g. "am I free Friday?").</td></tr>
        <tr><td class="c"><code>help me prepare for my meeting</code></td><td class="d">Get briefed and ready for an upcoming meeting.</td></tr>
        <tr><td class="c"><code>my profile</code></td><td class="d">See your own details, like your email address.</td></tr>
      </tbody></table></div>
    </div>

    <div class="cmdgroup span-2">
      <div class="gh"><div class="gi"><img src="data:image/png;base64," alt="Mela"></div><div><h3>Anytime</h3><p class="gsub">If you're ever unsure</p></div></div>
      <div class="tablewrap"><table><tbody>
        <tr><td class="c"><code>help</code></td><td class="d">Show what Mela can do. In a group or channel, use <code>@mela help</code>.</td></tr>
      </tbody></table></div>
    </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- ============ FAQ ============ -->
  <section id="faq">
    <span class="sec-label">Questions</span>
    <h2>Frequently asked</h2>
    <p class="sec-intro">The things people ask most about using Mela.</p>
    <div class="faq">

      <details>
        <summary>Do I need to sign in to use Mela?</summary>
        <p>No. You can add Mela to meetings and see this help without signing in. Retrieving stored transcripts and summaries requires your organization to have an active Armely account, which your Microsoft 365 admin sets up during onboarding.</p>
      </details>

      <details>
        <summary>How do I start recording a meeting?</summary>
        <p>Join the Teams meeting, then in the meeting chat type <code>@mela please join</code>. Mela joins the call, announces that it's transcribing, and starts taking notes. To stop, type <code>@mela please leave</code> (or just <code>@mela leave</code>).</p>
      </details>

      <details>
        <summary>Does everyone know the meeting is being transcribed?</summary>
        <p>Yes. When Mela joins, it posts a notice in the meeting chat and shows a recording indicator, so every participant knows notes are being taken. There's nothing hidden.</p>
      </details>

      <details>
        <summary>Can I pause Mela during a sensitive part of the meeting?</summary>
        <p>Yes. Type <code>@mela pause recording</code> to stop taking notes, then <code>@mela unpause recording</code> to resume. If it stays paused, Mela reminds you after about 5 minutes so you don't forget to turn it back on.</p>
      </details>

      <details>
        <summary>Mela isn't responding in my channel — why?</summary>
        <p>In a team channel, Microsoft Teams only delivers messages that <em>mention</em> the bot. Start your message with <code>@Mela</code> (for example <code>@mela help</code>) and it will respond. In direct and group chats you don't need the mention.</p>
      </details>

      <details>
        <summary>Can I get the summary sent to my email?</summary>
        <p>Yes. Ask Mela to <code>send the last summary to my email</code>, or add "…and email it to me" when you request a summary, transcript, or minutes. Mela delivers it to your inbox.</p>
      </details>

      <details>
        <summary>Can I get a private one-page executive summary?</summary>
        <p>Yes. Type <code>@mela send me the executive summary</code> (or <code>exec summary</code> / <code>one-pager</code>) and Mela emails a one-page summary — TL;DR, decisions, action items, risks, and next steps — to <strong>you only</strong>. It's never posted in the meeting chat, so it's safe to request from a group conversation. You can even ask <strong>during the meeting</strong> — Mela builds it from the live transcript captured up to that point.</p>
      </details>

      <details>
        <summary>Where are my transcripts stored, and are they secure?</summary>
        <p>Transcripts and summaries are encrypted both in transit and at rest, in storage scoped to your organization. See our <a href="#">Security &amp; Privacy</a> page for the full details on how your data is handled.</p>
      </details>

      <details>
        <summary>What language does Mela work in?</summary>
        <p>Mela transcribes in your organization's configured language — English (en-US) by default. If your team needs another language, contact <a href="#">support</a> and we'll help set it up.</p>
      </details>

      <details>
        <summary>How do I get Mela for my whole organization?</summary>
        <p>Your Microsoft 365 administrator completes a short onboarding to connect your tenant and grant the required permissions. Learn more at <a href="https://armely.com/mela-meeting-assistant">armely.com/mela-meeting-assistant</a>.</p>
